:"CVE-2026-103531","title":"A flaw has been found in OpenSC up to 0.27.1.","desc":"A flaw has been found in OpenSC up to 0.27.1. The impacted element is the function setcos_construct_fci_44 of the file src/libopensc/card-setcos.c. Executing a manipulation of the argument type_attr can lead to stack-based buffer overflow. The attack can be launched remotely. This patch is called ad730304052937c32b4eb489a06835ac6123632c. It is best practice to apply a patch to resolve this issue.","score":5.1,"sev":"medium","published":"2026-10-01T01:16:35.963","modified":"2026-10-01T01:16:35.963","window_date":"2026-10-01","activity_at":"2026-10-01T01:16:35.963","date_basis":"CVE publication","affected":[],"refs":[{"label":"NVD record","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-103531","source":"NVD"},{"label":"CVE Program record","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-103531","source":"CVE Program"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/OpenSC/OpenSC/","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/OpenSC/OpenSC/commit/ad730304052937c32b4eb489a06835ac6123632c","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/OpenSC/OpenSC/pull/3812","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-103531","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://vuldb.com/submit/956910","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://vuldb.com/vuln/412343","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://vuldb.com/vuln/412343/cti","source":"NVD"}],"related_cves":[],"advisories":[],"sources":["NVD"],"kev":null,"primary_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-103531"},{"id":"CVE-2026-103530","title":"A vulnerability was detected in decolua 9Router up to 0.5.55.","desc":"A vulnerability was detected in decolua 9Router up to 0.5.55. The affected element is the function fetch of the file src/shared/utils/ssrfGuard.js of the component Search Endpoint. Performing a manipulation of the argument provider_options.baseUrl results in server-side request forgery. The attack can be initiated remotely. Applying a patch is the recommended action to fix this issue.","score":6.9,"sev":"medium","published":"2026-10-01T00:16:43.287","modified":"2026-10-01T00:16:44.563","window_date":"2026-10-01","activity_at":"2026-10-01T00:32:50Z","date_basis":"GitHub advisory publication","affected":[],"refs":[{"label":"NVD record","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-103530","source":"NVD"},{"label":"CVE Program record","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-103530","source":"CVE Program"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/decolua/9router/","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/decolua/9router/issues/3714","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://github.com/decolua/9router/pull/3723","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-103530","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://vuldb.com/submit/956865","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://vuldb.com/vuln/412342","source":"NVD"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://vuldb.com/vuln/412342/cti","source":"NVD"},{"label":"GitHub security advisory","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-ggrj-5337-qvwm","source":"GitHub"},{"label":"Advisory reference","url":"https://github.com/decolua/9router","source":"GitHub"}],"related_cves":[],"advisories":[{"label":"GitHub Security Advisory","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-ggrj-5337-qvwm"}],"sources":["NVD","GitHub Advisory Database"],"kev":null,"primary_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-103530"},{"id":"CVE-2026-101283","title":"iperf3 3.20–3.21 (esnet/iperf) has a pre-auth heap buffer overflow in decrypt_rsa_message(): a 256-byte RSA buffer is BIO_read with the attacker-controlled ciphertext length (guard","desc":"iperf3 3.20–3.21 (esnet/iperf) has a pre-auth heap buffer overflow in decrypt_rsa_message(): a 256-byte RSA buffer is BIO_read with the attacker-controlled ciphertext length (guard warns only), so an unauthenticated client overflows the heap via an oversized authtoken; fixed in 3.22","score":9.2,"sev":"critical","published":"2026-09-30T22:16:33.317","modified":"2026-09-30T22:16:33.317","window_date":"2026-10-01","activity_at":"2026-10-01T00:32:49Z","date_basis":"GitHub advisory publication","affected":[],"refs":[{"label":"NVD record","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-101283","source":"NVD"},{"label":"CVE Program record","url":"https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-101283","source":"CVE Program"},{"label":"Reference","url":"https://newreleases.io/project/github/esnet/iperf/release/3.22","source":"NVD"},{"label":"GitHub security advisory","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-pwcx-5qh6-2pxc","source":"GitHub"}],"related_cves":[],"advisories":[{"label":"GitHub Security Advisory","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-pwcx-5qh6-2pxc"}],"sources":["NVD","GitHub Advisory Database"],"kev":null,"primary_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-101283"},{"id":"CVE-2025-9989","title":"The Broadstreet plugin for WordPress is vulnerable to Stored Cross-Site Scripting via admin...","desc":"The Broadstreet plugin for WordPress is vulnerable to Stored Cross-Site Scripting via admin settings in all versions up to, and including, 1.53.1 due to insufficient input sanitization and output escaping. This makes it possible for authenticated attackers, with administrator-level permissions and above, to inject arbitrary web scripts in pages that will execute whenever a user accesses an injected page. This only affects multi-site installations and installations where unfiltered_html has been disabled.","score":4.4,"sev":"medium","published":"2026-05-13T05:16:13Z","modified":null,"window_date":"2026-10-01","activity_at":"2026-10-01T00:32:48Z","date_basis":"GitHub advisory publication","affected":[],"refs":[{"label":"GitHub security advisory","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-7c33-q787-xg22","source":"GitHub"},{"l